      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your feelings of existential dread are a common and deeply human response to the vast, often silent silence of the universe. Many philosophers, from the absurdists to the stoics, suggest that meaning isn't something we find, but rather something we create for ourselves. The struggle itself can be a way to define our character and give life value, even in the absence of a grand design.",
      "source": "target",
